plugin-hostd (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * You choose which program runs LV2 plugins: mod-host, omx-clap-host or
    auto (the setting lv2_worker, changed with the lv2_worker_set command).
    A host that cannot take LV2 plugins now answers with a new error (-512)
    and the daemon announces the refusal with the lv2_adapter_refused event.
  * omx-clap-host 0.9.0 or newer is recommended: older versions do not load
    LV2 plugins, so with the default auto choice everything would run on
    mod-host.
  * A new page explains how to use plugin-hostd in your own host.
  * Fixed a build failure of programs that include pin.h with gcc -O3
    -Werror.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

plugin-hostd (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New package plugin-hostd-tests ships the fake worker (fake-host) in
    /usr/libexec/plugin-hostd/tests/, so the CI of other repositories can
    run the pin-file test for real.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000

plugin-hostd (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pins are learned on first use: the first time a plugin is added its pin
    is recorded in a pin store, and a later change of the plugin or its
    layout is announced instead of passing silently.
  * pin_file names the pin store; saves are fsync'd so a crash never loses a
    pin, and a corrupt or overlong store line is refused rather than trusted.
  * One format table holds a row per plugin format: the pins and the
    supervisor read the row, so a new format needs no changes elsewhere, and
    the protocol names capabilities instead of formats.
  * The packages require omx-clap-host-tests as a floor only, no ceiling.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

